<main id="main" class="community-shell"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>What this website uses and displays.</h1><p class="page-intro">This page describes the LineClash website and its community directory. Individual game servers are operated separately.</p>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Public game information</h2><p>Participating servers report their public address, name, availability and population. Reported match history can include nicknames, teams, results, gameplay statistics and replay events. This information appears in the server browser, statistics, player pages and public API.</p><p>Local nicknames belong to each server; central account handles appear as @handle across servers. Choose a nickname you are comfortable displaying publicly. For questions about a reported match, contact the operator of the server that submitted it.</p></section>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Central accounts</h2><p>Creating an account stores your username, private email address, account identifier, creation time and password hash. Native login sessions are stored as token hashes and expire after twelve hours; connection approvals expire after five minutes. Client PIN sign-in requests store a short PIN, client type, expiry and the hash of a separate private device secret. PINs expire after five minutes and expired records are removed when new requests are created. Approved requests are linked to your account. Network addresses are hashed for request limiting. Emails are used for sign-in and are not displayed publicly or sent to game servers. When the operator enables email verification, new accounts must confirm a single-use activation link before signing in. Verification tokens are stored only as hashes, expire after 24 hours and are deleted after confirmation. Requests to resend links are rate-limited. Existing accounts retain access; with verification disabled, new registration does not confirm email ownership. When SMTP is configured, a password recovery request sends a reset link to the registered email address through the configured mail relay. Only a hash of that single-use token is stored; the link expires after 30 minutes and is deleted after a successful reset. Recovery is disabled when SMTP is not configured. Passwords and reusable central sessions are never sent to participating game servers. Servers receive your verified account identifier and handle and retain control of their local permissions, bans and records.</p></section>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Profile changes and deletion</h2><p>Sign in to Account to change your email or password. Changes require your current password. When email verification is required, a new address is confirmed before replacing the current one; pending change tokens expire after 24 hours. Completed changes invalidate other sign-ins.</p><p>You can permanently delete your central account by confirming your password and typing DELETE. The live website removes your account, email, password hash and sign-in/reset/activation tokens. Your name is removed from individual leaderboards and displayed as DELETED PLAYER in retained match results and replays. Numeric scores, placements, wins and team results remain, with separate anonymous participant records. A team label containing personal identity text is replaced with a non-name label. Replays are edited to remove names and their published checksums are updated.</p><p>This operation covers the live central website. Independently operated game servers, their local accounts and logs, already downloaded files, client-saved names and offline backups have separate retention. Operational logs and unlinked source-rate counters follow the site's retention policy. Contact the relevant operator for those records. Retained gameplay traces may still be recognizable from information held elsewhere.</p></section>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Website requests</h2><p>The Account page uses a secure session cookie for sign-in and connection approvals. The website does not include an analytics script. The hosting server may record ordinary access and error logs, including request details and network addresses; log retention is controlled by the site operator.</p><p>Fonts load from Google Fonts. The download section requests public release information from GitHub. Your browser connects to those services, which receive the network information needed to answer the requests. Following an external link is governed by the destination’s own privacy practices.</p></section>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Your device</h2><p>Copy buttons use the clipboard when you click them. Screenshot previews and the animated background run in your browser. The game separately saves local settings and server entries on your device; the last signed-in central username and email address are also kept locally. Passwords and native login sessions are not saved to disk by the client.</p></section>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Questions</h2><p>Use Account for central-account deletion. For other website data or retention requests, contact the site operator. <a href="https://github.com/frossmant">Project maintainer</a>. Avoid posting passwords, tokens or personal information in public issues.</p></section></main><?php site_footer(); ?>
